From 1b8b5fb9411715fa89762ea1b6773ed119cdfdf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jky72 <jky72@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:32:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] perf(shader): let a slow integrated GPU pick its own
 background scale

The divisor used to come from the window size alone, which cannot tell a fast integrated GPU from
a slow one: a 1080p window scaled nothing at all, and a 4K one always stopped at half. It now
follows the frame rate. Frames below 50fps for three seconds in a row step it coarser, up to a
quarter resolution, and the search restarts from the resolution floor when the window is resized.
It never steps back finer: the two-way version hunted between two scales every four seconds on a
Radeon iGPU (2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 3 -> 2 ...), which re-created the render target each time and made the
background visibly change size.

Measured on a Radeon integrated GPU at 3840x2160, one shader, animation on: it settles at divisor
3 (1280x720 background) after a single step from 23fps, and stops there. Unit tests cover the
floor, the division and the latch.
